We need to parse the comment:

```
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the list), then for every position i greater than the index and less than the old size of the list minus one, either both the current and the old value at position i+1 are null, or the current value at position i equals the old value at position i+1.
```

We need to express: If index is valid (0 <= index < old size), then for all i such that i > index && i < \old(this.size()) - 1 (since old size minus one). Wait: "less than the old size of the list minus one" means i < oldSize - 1. Since i is greater than index and less than oldSize -1. For each such i, either both current and old value at position i+1 are null, or current value at position i equals old value at position i+1.

We need to use observers: get(i) returns element at index i. Also we have size() method. Use \old(this.size()) for old size. Use this.get(i) for current. Use \old(this.get(i+1)) for old value at i+1.

